  :step-1 {:clause [:?msg "hasCreator" :?f]              :per-binding 2.592 :grouped 3.240 :out 910}
  :step-2 {:clause [:?msg "message/creationDate" :?date] :per-binding 3.043 :grouped 4.032 :out 910}
  :sum-per-binding 7.208}

 :the-gap
 "The three join steps total 7.2 ms. The paired benchmark on the same dataset
  reports IC02 at 47.5 ms p50 for kotobase. Planning is no longer the answer --
  it is 2.3 ms on the heavier IC09 two-hop since kotobase-peer ea13f73 -- so
  roughly 40 ms of IC02 is somewhere other than clause joining or planning.
  Naming that place is the next measurement, and this receipt deliberately does
  not guess at it: the last time someone reasoned about IC02 instead of
  measuring it, the resulting change made IC02 monotonically worse across three
  runs (2026-08-02-ldbc-snb-ic02-hypothesis-refuted.edn)."

 :a-trap-worth-recording
 "An ad-hoc probe written to split IC02 into plan / execute / harness-top-20
  reported plan 0.136 ms, execute 0.810 ms, full query 0.615 ms -- numbers that
  would have looked like a discovery. It also printed `rows 0`. The query was
  matching nothing, and every one of those timings was of an empty answer.

  It was caught only because the probe printed a row count, a habit acquired
  earlier the same day after the LDBC Interactive Short harness was found timing
  zero-row queries and reporting them as measurements. A benchmark that cannot
  tell `fast` from `found nothing` will eventually report the second as the
  first, and a hand-written probe is a benchmark."

 :what-changed-since-the-refuted-hypothesis
 {:ic02-paired-ratio {:2026-08-02-median-quotient 19.2 :2026-08-13-paired 9.710}
  :note "Different statistics -- a quotient of separately-summarised medians then,
         a per-sample paired ratio now -- so the two are not strictly comparable.
         The direction is clear and the magnitude is not."}

 :next
 "Instrument the engine's own execute for IC02, the way ic09-diag instruments
  planning: measure inside `datalog.core/q`, not around it. A probe that rebuilds
  the query outside the engine can be wrong in ways the engine cannot."}
